{"stage": "step:s1", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2219, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2219, "model": null, "output_tokens": 580, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 580, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "content": [{"text": "I read all six project documents. They give no latency figures for any candidate, so latency on the Level-1 FPGA is still unknown.\n\n**Candidates** (`candidate_specs.md`)\n- **Algorithm-L1:** iterative topological clustering with a learned calibration.\n- **Algorithm-L3:** sliding-window clustering with a learned calibration.\n- **Algorithm-L2:** fixed-window sum.\n- The spec lists no tunable parameters other than the trigger threshold, which the task brief limits to 20\u201360 GeV.\n- The spec says all three fit the FPGA resource budget (LUTs, DSPs). It says nothing about latency.\n\n**Allocated rate** (`rate_allocation.md`): 8 kHz of Level-1 bandwidth.\n\n**Earlier emulation** (`simulation_summary_2025.md`, 35 GeV threshold only): signal efficiency at the allocated rate was 92% for L1, 85% for L3 and 74% for L2.\n\n**Other documents:** the meeting notes, schedule and links documents have nothing on latency. The optical links have enough bandwidth for all candidates. The firmware freeze is in Q4.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The 4.0 \u00b5s latency limit is a hard requirement, and no document shows whether any candidate meets it. Iterative clustering (L1) could plausibly be the slowest, but that is my guess and no document supports it. It needs checking before L1 is recommended, even though L1 had the best efficiency.\n- The efficiency figures are from 2025 at one threshold. They need re-running across thresholds with `simulate_efficiency`.\n\nI recorded the 8 kHz rate, the 4.0 \u00b5s limit and the three 2025 efficiencies.", "type": "text"}]}
